\newlabel{fig:stability maps}{{3}{19}{Affine projection stability maps displaying the number of negative eigenvalues of the chemical and coherent Gibbs energy Hessian for BCC\textsubscript {A2} in the \ch {Hf-Nb-Ti-V} system at (a,b)~\SI {600}{\kelvin }, (c,d)~\SI {800}{\kelvin }, and (e,f)~\SI {1000}{\kelvin }. Left column: chemical Hessian; right column: coherent Hessian. Coherent strain suppresses the spinodal most strongly in Hf- and V-rich compositions across all temperatures}{figure.caption.77}{}}
